Trace-only copy. benchGenerator activates tracing only for the selected yielded callback, after the original per-child calibration; benchFn adds 20 untimed callbacks after its original first-call/conditional-warmup block in the warmed arm and records each raw sample before the original sort/trim. Worker retains childMain/runTrialAt/calibration and writes trace after a causal setImmediate GC-observer drain. Forced GC before/after each sample is marked separately from callback spans. GC PerformanceObserver records are drained with takeRecords before disconnect, but GC event capture may still be incomplete if an event is not observable by that point. Both arms replay the saved 20-sample plan. No result arithmetic, callback body, GC setting, trim, or benchmark output path changes. CPU counters are process-wide and may include background threads. Tracing perturbs timing and is diagnostic only.
